.TH "TRCC\-CONFIG" "1" "" "trcc\-linux 9.8.3" "TRCC Manual"
.SH NAME
trcc\-config \- App\-global preferences: temp unit, language, GPU, refresh interval
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrcc config\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
App\-global preferences: temp unit, language, GPU, refresh interval.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS date\-format
.PP
\fBtrcc config date\-format\fR \fIFMT\fR
.PP
Set the global LCD overlay date format.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBFMT\fR
LCD date format, e.g. 'yyyy/MM/dd', 'dd.MM.yyyy', 'MM/dd/yyyy'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS gpu
.PP
\fBtrcc config gpu\fR [\fIKEY\fR]
.PP
Pick the primary GPU for sensor overlays. Empty string = auto.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
GPU sensor key (e.g. 'nvidia:0') or '' to clear
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS language
.PP
\fBtrcc config language\fR \fILANG\fR
.PP
Set the UI language.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBLANG\fR
ISO 639\-1 code, e.g. 'en', 'zh', 'fr'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS refresh\-interval
.PP
\fBtrcc config refresh\-interval\fR \fISECONDS\fR
.PP
Set the global metrics\-refresh / render\-and\-send tick interval.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBSECONDS\fR
Seconds between metric refreshes (1 to 100)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS temp\-unit
.PP
\fBtrcc config temp\-unit\fR \fIUNIT\fR
.PP
Set the global temperature unit (propagates to every device).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBUNIT\fR
Either 'C' or 'F'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS time\-format
.PP
\fBtrcc config time\-format\fR \fIFMT\fR
.PP
Set the global LCD overlay clock format.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBFMT\fR
LCD clock format: '12h' or '24h'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtrcc\fR(1)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report bugs at \fBhttps://github.com/Lexonight1/thermalright-trcc-linux/issues\fR \(em include the output of \fBtrcc report\fR.
